# K17-R — one lease law on the realm boards: the Episkopos brief (controller, 2026-10-26)

Mask: **Realm-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)**, the K17-R Episkopos, fresh lane. Wave D landed (PR #95, span 43bdc025f),
so this lane opens on its ground.

## Read first, in order
1. `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem`: stand the whole house.
2. `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem` #/the-lane-law (binds you) and
   `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem` (#/the-seats, #/the-shapes, #/the-launch, #/the-fences).
3. `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane.mem`: the lane kit, the mandate (operator rulings on forks
   3 and 4, 2026-10-22) and its five slices R1–R5, landed WHOLE in one lane.
4. `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem` (what Wave C built: `lease-advance`, `hand-lineage`, the
   quorum act, `readWideningFrontier`) and road rows `K17` plus the edge-frontier ruling in
   `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem` (grep "The edge frontier").

## Ground
- Worktree: `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k17-r/wt`, branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--k17-r`, head 43bdc025f
  (provisioned and stamped). Build there; never the main tree. `git config core.bare` reads `false` before and after.
- Your FIRST act: survey (one walled `gpt-6-luna` reader, or yourself) every site the five slices touch: the unsigned
  max-register (`effectiveLeaseEpoch`, `rollLeaseEpochOnBoard` and their fixtures), the `nexus-rekey` writer, the
  herm's raise door (`effectiveLeaseEpochOnBoard`), `cabal-join`, the vessel standing, the realm clock, `memberAside`,
  `standsInRealm`, the vouch edges. Then write the file set you hold into `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k17-r/resume.md`
  before any build. You leave alone: the span, `main`, every other lane's files (W28's `face-gate*`, `gate-*`,
  `face-dial` belong to the w28-gate lane), genesis, the boot seed.

## The mandate you enact
- ONE lease law: every lease epoch rises only on a signed advance. A face advances by its per-writer signed slot under
  its KEL lineage (Wave C, already built). A Nexus or cabal-realm advance signs as a `QuorumAct` at the roster's
  threshold under its own epoch's lineage.
- The unsigned max-register retires ENTIRELY; the signed path stands alone. Its fixtures migrate to signed fixtures
  through the real founding path. No shim, no dual reader, no old-name alias (an old-name refusal lives one commit, then
  burns).
- The realm boards' frontiers widen K17 the same way the fleet board's do: the charter quorum hand signs its stream's
  frontier, and the realm readers widen only as of a qualifying frontier, waiting as unknown where none qualifies.
- No clock decides anything; a wait finds the product's own causal event.
- Reds first, each with a control. Required reds:
  1. an unsigned `rollLeaseEpochOnBoard` advance on a realm raises nothing (CONTROL: a threshold hand raises it);
  2. a sub-threshold hand raises nothing;
  3. an older epoch's advance verifies under the seal-roll chain's keys, and a forged lineage refuses;
  4. a realm reader acting before any qualifying frontier waits as unknown (CONTROL: after the frontier, it acts as of it,
     its receipt naming it);
  5. silent-zero: any census that reads "no unsigned site left" proves itself first on a planted site.

## Crew (mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes; operator rulings 2026-10-28, groups A and B)
- The default Codex crew: a Sonnet Episkopos, one `gpt-6.1-terra` BUILDER (walled, medium effort, `-s workspace-write
  -C <worktree> --add-dir <seat-dir>`), one `gpt-6-luna` READER and sweeper at HIGH effort (walled, `-s read-only
  -C <seat-dir>`). A slice touching caps, custody, crypto, the gate or Keyhive also gets a `gpt-6.1-sol` read at high.
  `gpt-6-sol` never launches (6.1 only). No seat launches `--ephemeral`. No Opus builder seat by default: an Opus seat
  only on a named seam slice, with the reason in the brief.
- Before any Codex launch, read the pool: `python3 /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/spend.py` prints the pool line;
  at or below the 20% floor, launch no new Codex seat and hand back instead.
- Seat dirs under the lane's own `seats/`. Launch exactly as mixed-model-swarm#/the-launch (`--search` before `exec`;
  `< /dev/null`; the handback in out.md, `-o` to final.md). Terra builds and writes reds; Luna reads each slice before
  it pushes and runs the aftermath sweep; YOU run suites and read every build as the second lineage.
- Background runs go through the harness's background mode; arm your own marker-file watch
  (`until [ -f <seat>/final.md ]`) so a spirit's finish wakes you. Never `pgrep -f`. Never read a credential file.

## Battery and landing
- Then: `pnpm build` (stamps); each touched package's WHOLE suite under a scratch HOME and scratch LAR_ROOT, LAR_BAGS unset
  (lararium-mesh's suite always, since its census tests read every package's source); `node --test tools/*.test.mjs`;
  `tools/witness-all.sh`; `node tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs`. At most one e2e file locally; the whole e2e set runs on
  CI shards. Push the lane branch; read `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --branch <lane> --head <full sha>`. CI and held-out
  must both read green.
- Commits: `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`, subject `lar:///ha.ka.ba/<pkg>/<area>/<w1.w2.w3> — summary`,
  trailers `Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`, `Co-Authored-By: Codex gpt-6-sol` for Sol's
  work, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NRJJL73CYwoGfShMujgUHQ`.
- Canon in the same burst: the kit's #/the-slices reads what stands, each slice built; re-stamp with
  `LAR_ROOT=<scratch> node packages/lares-cli/bin/lares.mjs meme normalize <file>` (the second pass reads canonical).
  The controller writes the road row at the land; you do not edit the road.

## Fences
No `git stash` in any form; no `--no-verify`; no `.git/config`; never push `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` or `main`;
never `git worktree remove --force`; no foreground `sleep`; a refused command stops that step: save a patch, hand back.
Clock waits: find the product's own event, never raise a timeout. Never "family" for a PersonaGroup.

## Hand-back
Hand back ONCE (the controller reads it the first time; never resend). One `<<~ status "…">>` line, then: slices BUILT /
OWED, commits with full shas, CI and held-out verdicts on the final head, suites read, the reader's findings and how
each closed, canon lines, slips and refusals. Keep `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k17-r/resume.md` current, one line per
step, so a relaunch can take the lane. Stop there; the controller trains and lands K17-R.

## Swarm refinements (operator-approved, 2026-10-28; bind every lane from now)
1. A controller ruling on behavior carries a measure (a grep, one test it ran) or arrives marked LEAN: verify before building, and push back with evidence when the code says otherwise.
2. Slice cap: a slice lands as its own PR once its plan stands built and read. A finding that widens scope goes to the next slice's brief, never into the slice in flight.
3. Red first, by order: the red lands as its own commit before the fix commit, so a reader sees the red's sha fail on its parent. A red written after its fix names that and carries a proof run against the parent.
4. Before each push, run ONE e2e file locally that exercises the surface the lane touched (the disk law allows one); name it in the hand-back. The whole e2e set still runs on CI shards only.
5. The reader's findings go straight to the builder's Episkopos; the controller reads the copy and rules only on forks (design, scope, law).
6. One writer per worktree. No claims ledger: `.lane-claims.md` retired as design crud; never create it.
7. Spend reads from what each tool writes, never from a seat's own word: the controller runs `python3 /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/spend.py --lane <lane> [--since <date>]`, which tallies Claude subagent transcripts (usage per message, helpers billed to their parent), Codex rollouts (`~/.codex/sessions`, lane from the rollout's cwd) and Copilot run logs (their closing `Requests N Premium` line). So every Codex seat launches WITHOUT `--ephemeral` (an ephemeral run writes no rollout and goes uncounted), and every seat's cwd sits under the lane's own scratch directory. A hand-back names its seats; the numbers come from the script.

