/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:43:| ''Fresh reader'' | a lineage that built nothing in the piece, read-only | an adversarial read of a whole lane before its train, findings ranked with `file:line` | sees the builder's conclusions first |
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:50:!! The shapes ~ how a crew stands
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:52:* ''The work swarm.'' A lane runs a Sonnet Episkopos with enacting seats: the Terra builds, the Luna reads and sweeps, a Sol joins only for a named deep question, and the Copilot seat reads the batch's Aftermath. A Copilot build costs several times a Copilot read against a fixed monthly allowance, so builds go to the Terra. Terra, Luna, Sol and `gpt-5.3-codex` share the OpenAI lineage, so their cross-read counts once, and the Episkopos reads every build as the second lineage. A seat never reads a diff it wrote.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:53:* ''The build pair.'' The building seats share ONE worktree the lead provisions, with ONE writer at a time, so their work composes as it lands. A seat that needs to write in parallel works in a worktree of its own, and the lead merges from it. The lead pulls the work by diff, reads it and lands it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:54:* ''A short lineage keeps its seat.'' When the operator names a lineage short, its seats pass to another lineage's models of the same capability, and the lens law still sorts who reads whom; the operator names the shortfall's end the same way. Where Codex stands absent, a lane runs an Opus Episkopos with an Opus and a Sonnet spirit trading builder, reviewer and sweeper masks.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:55:* ''Crew law.'' Seven refinements bind every lane (operator, 2026-10-28):
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:56:** A controller ruling on behavior carries a measure (a grep, one test it ran) or arrives marked LEAN; the lane verifies before building and pushes back with evidence when the code says otherwise.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:60:** A reader's findings go straight to the builder's Episkopos; the controller reads the copy and rules only on forks (design, scope, law).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:61:** One writer per worktree; no claims ledger.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:62:** Spend reads from what each tool writes, never from a seat's own word: the controller runs `python3 /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/spend.py --lane <lane> [--since <date>]`, which tallies Claude subagent transcripts, Codex rollouts and Copilot run logs. A hand-back names its seats and their models; the numbers come from the script.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:64:* ''The Chao of a review'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/chao">>). Two reads over one question wear the Chao's two faces, and the review resolves to three:
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:68:* ''Overwatch.'' The Opus controller reads every crew's handback and every chunk's diff before it merges, and names each finding it would block on. Work that moves a fact between processes or threads (a writer and its readers, a composer and its islands, a verb and its route) always takes the controller's own read of the crossing, since a module's own reads catch its contract and miss its crossings.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:69:* ''The battery runs at the wave's end, on the shards.'' A wave writes every red and its control as it builds, since a red names the specification, and runs nothing between its fixes. At its end it runs locally only what CI cannot: the build, and each red's proof against its base (the red files alone over the pre-cure tree). It pushes once, and CI carries the battery: the lane CI runs every package suite, the witnesses and the tool self-tests; `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>` spreads both e2e sets across shards; held-out runs its cells. The wave reads every verdict, cures what reads red, pushes again only once no run flies, and hands back when CI and held-out read green.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:70:* ''The fresh read and the train.'' A lane's handback takes a fresh reader's whole-lane read before it merges; a HOLD sends the findings back as the next launch, up to five launches, with the uncertainties talked out between them. The controller then merges ready lanes in trains (#/the-lanes).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:83:# ''Measure over agree.'' Where eyes disagree, a probe, a red test or a repeated run settles it; a vote never does.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:91:GitHub Copilot reaches models the Codex budget never spends. Nothing the house gates on needs it to pass.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:100:!!! Its fences
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:101:# ''One launcher'', `tools/launch-copilot.mjs read|build`, its walls pinned by `tools/launch-copilot.test.mjs`. Both modes run with no URL, no built-in MCP server (the GitHub server reaches the network and writes), no system temp directory, no prompt and no auto-update, stdin closed and `COPILOT_ALLOW_ALL` dropped; a seat whose working directory sits in the system temp directory refuses, since the temp wall blinds it there. The seat's handback, log and share land in its seat directory.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:103:# ''Walled when it builds'' (`build`, where a build must go to Copilot): file writes in the lane's build worktree alone, `npx vitest` and `npx tsc` there; every git write, push, network fetch, `rm`, `mv`, `npm` and `pnpm` denied; it refuses the main checkout, a directory that holds no worktree, and a missing or in-checkout `LAR_ROOT`, refuses `--add-dir`, and drops any `LAR_BAGS`. A launch never widens these walls (no `shell(bash)`, no `shell(env)`, never `--allow-all-*` or `--yolo`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:113:!! The lanes ~ a sub-branch, a pull request, a train
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:116:* ''A lane hands back on green'': its battery reads green on its own CI and held-out (#/the-shapes, the battery), its pull request opens into the work branch, and its fresh read follows.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:118:* ''The controller merges in trains'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff">> #/state): it reads the span's own head green first, merges ready lanes onto one scratch head, runs one crucible over the combined tree (the shared packages' suites, both whole e2e sets, `tools/witness-all.sh`), places canon, and pushes the span once, through a gate that refuses while any run flies.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:126:A lane closes with an o-takiage pass before its pull request opens, and the controller closes each settle with one over everything it landed. The rite returns rather than discards: git keeps the ashes, and the tree reads as if the new shape had always stood.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:128:# ''Burn only what a later carrier or module plainly superseded'': an old message kind, a dead dial, a scaffold test, a stale comment. Unwired work no landed lane superseded stays; doubt goes on an ask list.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:131:# ''Testimony stays.'' A testimony carrier, a dated scout and a dated crossing row keep their words; the house re-trues their frame, never their body.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:134:# ''Scratch returns too.'' A seat's worktree leaves only after a census proves every file it holds landed; plain `git worktree remove`, never `--force`; a worktree that initialized submodules waits for the operator's hand.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:138:<<~ ahu #/the-fences>>
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:140:!! The fences ~ every lineage keeps them
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:142:* ''One writer per lane.'' Seats of any lineage write only inside their own worktree; the Episkopos alone lands, from its own tree, with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:143:* ''A refused command stops that step'' for every lineage alike: never retried, reshaped, split, moved to another tool, or handed to another seat (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff">> #/the-lane-law).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:145:* ''A build reads its own tree'': a provisioned checkout whose links resolve inside it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:147:* ''The disk carries; the seat re-reads.'' A spirit runs outside its overseer's budget, so an outage (a rate limit, a crash, a compaction) stops the watcher and never the work: the spirit finishes its brief and its handback lands on disk unread, its build dirty in the worktree. The Episkopos writes its resume sheet at each commit and before each spirit launch, naming the spirit's directory and `out.md`, so a re-awakened seat reads what the spirit left and never mistakes it for stray work.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:148:* ''A shard run reads the head it names.'' `node tools/e2e-shards.mjs push <lane>` pushes the HEAD of the checkout it runs from, so it runs from the lane's own worktree, and the run's `headSha` reads before its colour.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:157:* ''The walled Codex seat'': `cd <dir> && TMPDIR=<dir>/.tmp TMPPREFIX=<dir>/.tmp/zsh codex exec -m gpt-6.1-terra -c model_reasoning_effort=medium -s workspace-write -c sandbox_workspace_write.exclude_slash_tmp=true -c sandbox_workspace_write.exclude_tmpdir_env_var=true --skip-git-repo-check -C <dir> -o <dir>/final.md "<brief>" < /dev/null`, in the background. A builder (`gpt-6.1-terra`, medium effort) runs `-C <worktree> --add-dir <dir>`; a reader (`gpt-6-luna`, medium effort, `-s read-only`) runs `-C <dir>` over an empty directory and reads the repo from there. The walls keep `/tmp` and every other worktree unwritable, the seat's temp files live inside its own directory, and `workspace-write` keeps `gh` reachable where `read-only` reaches no network.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:158:* ''Every seat keeps its rollout.'' No Codex seat launches with `--ephemeral`: an ephemeral run writes no rollout and goes uncounted, and a seat cut short continues by its session id (`codex exec resume <id> -m <model> -c model_reasoning_effort=<level>`), and the lead's resume sheet records that id beside the seat's directory, model, effort and head. Each seat's `-C` directory sits under the lane's own scratch directory, since the spend script finds the lane from the rollout's cwd.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:163:* ''A walled seat builds and never runs suites'': vitest, pnpm and tsx each break behind the walls, so the seat builds modules and writes reds and controls, and the lead runs the build and the red proofs.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:167:* ''A Copilot read names its target'': the branch, its head sha and the pull request, read through `git show <branch>:<path>` or the lane's own worktree, never the main tree. A paired read runs each face alone, then hands each its twin's handback.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:169:* ''The lead's own watch wakes it.'' A spirit's finish reaches its lead only through a watch the lead arms in the harness's background mode (`until [ -f <seat>/final.md ]`), never a watcher the spirit leaves behind; where a lead pauses on its own spirits, the controller arms that watch and messages the lead on the finish.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:170:* ''Owed probes'' (Sol's read of OpenAI's Codex docs, 2026-10-25, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/codex-controller-2026">>): a `--json` event stream ending on `turn.completed` as the watch's signal, `--output-schema` for a mechanical status beside `out.md`, a reader with command network off where its brief needs none, permission profiles in place of the flag list, and a matched A/B across Sol, a newer Sol and Luna; each lands here once measured on this host.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem:179:* A handback the house keeps lands verbatim as a testimony carrier, so no relaying hand rewrites it.
